  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=\u27e8-2,3\u27e9$ and $\\text{v}=\u27e84,-6\u27e9.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-6)-4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12-12 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$",
